WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.975
Chapter 08's architecture
is simple to draw.

2
00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:07.117
A branch query goes through the
SD-WAN edge to an agency resolver,

3
00:00:07.117 --> 00:00:10.790
into the policy plane, and on
to each cloud's private zones,

4
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:14.775
while internet lookups leave
through CISA's Protective DNS.

5
00:00:14.775 --> 00:00:20.300
Five decisions carry almost all of the
operational risk, and each fails silently:

6
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.000
the query still resolves, just outside
policy or to the wrong address.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.663
They are the redirect-dns destination,
the order of the forwarding chain,

8
00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:33.239
per-cloud conditional
forwarding, the AD DNS inventory,

9
00:00:33.239 --> 00:00:37.125
and reachability of the
certificate revocation endpoints.

10
00:00:37.125 --> 00:00:40.479
Each has a check you run
in the live configuration,

11
00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:44.487
not the design document, before
the next SD-WAN or DDI change.

12
00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:48.647
For example, resolve one name
per namespace from every origin;

13
00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:51.240
a public address means a missing rule.
